WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:56.350
<b>Rumors</b>

3
00:02:04.550 --> 00:02:05.460
What's that?!

4
00:02:05.490 --> 00:02:06.990
There's a gigantic Storm
called Aqua Laguna

5
00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:09.530
that's on its way
here right now?

6
00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:10.430
That's right!

7
00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:11.860
By midnight tonight
this entire beach

8
00:02:11.890 --> 00:02:13.800
will be completely
underwater as well as

9
00:02:13.830 --> 00:02:15.600
half of the town! Crazy, huh?

10
00:02:15.740 --> 00:02:18.080
That's terrible, we should
get out of here right away!

11
00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:19.270
Yes, sir, if we were smart,

12
00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:21.180
that's exactly what we would do!

13
00:02:21.210 --> 00:02:23.080
Let's evacuate to higher ground!

14
00:02:23.110 --> 00:02:24.950
Good idea, let's do that!

15
00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:27.920
Evacuate!

16
00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:33.020
Evacuate!

17
00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:44.180
[SANJI]
Run away!

18
00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:52.020
That's weird, I could've sworn
I heard someone out here.

19
00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:54.520
Be sure to evacuate!

20
00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:56.290
Evacuate, Usopp!

21
00:02:57.820 --> 00:03:00.850
They were saying
something about a storm?

22
00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:04.530
Well, actually the wind
is awfully strong, isn't it?

23
00:03:06.860 --> 00:03:07.560
Nami!

24
00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:08.630
I'm telling you people,

25
00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:12.030
we didn't do anything wrong,
you're making a mistake!

26
00:03:12.070 --> 00:03:14.270
And why should we
trust anything you say?

27
00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:18.440
You scumbags are pirates and probably
assassins, too!

28
00:03:18.470 --> 00:03:20.310
[LUFFY]
This doesn't
even make any sense!

29
00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:22.840
There's no reason why Robin would attack
him!

30
00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:24.380
Yeah! Not only that,

31
00:03:24.410 --> 00:03:28.420
we'd never even heard of Iceburg
until we met him yesterday!

32
00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:31.350
You brats just keep saying that all you
want.

33
00:03:31.390 --> 00:03:36.020
It's over. Fact is you
picked on the wrong guy.

34
00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:37.560
The moral of the story is,

35
00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:39.460
if you make an
enemy out of Iceburg.

36
00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:43.300
Then you make an enemy out
of the entire Galley-La Company.

37
00:03:43.330 --> 00:03:45.030
And that's not the half of it.

38
00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:46.900
You also made an
enemy out of everyone

39
00:03:46.930 --> 00:03:49.540
in this whole city,
you understand?

40
00:03:49.570 --> 00:03:51.570
Listen, I don't want to fight any of you!

41
00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:54.240
We can still talk
about all this, okay?!

42
00:03:54.270 --> 00:03:56.540
[PAULIE]
I don't give
a damn what you want!

43
00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:58.610
[CITIZEN I]
That's what you
get for messing with Galley-La!

44
00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:23.660
What's the matter, Straw Hat?

45
00:04:23.750 --> 00:04:26.790
You not even gonna
go out with a fight?

46
00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:27.990
I just told you.

47
00:04:28.020 --> 00:04:30.890
We're not enemies and I don't
want to fight any of you!

48
00:04:33.730 --> 00:04:35.360
[LULU]
Since pistols
don't work on you.

49
00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:37.800
We'll have to
go with Plan B.

50
00:04:40.370 --> 00:04:44.000
Damn it all. I guess these
guys are going all-out, huh?

51
00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:49.380
[CROWD cheers]

52
00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:52.280
[CITIZEN J]
Bulls-eye!

53
00:04:52.310 --> 00:04:54.360
[thinking]
No. He got away.

54
00:04:57.900 --> 00:04:59.900
Wow, they almost had me.

55
00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:29.700
Ah, uh-oh.
Can't dodge anymore.

56
00:05:35.410 --> 00:05:36.210
[CROWD cheers]

57
00:05:36.420 --> 00:05:37.860
[CITIZEN F]
All right, nice shot!

58
00:05:47.920 --> 00:05:49.390
Hahahaha!

59
00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:54.130
Yeah! And that's why
Galley-La is our pride and joy!

60
00:05:54.130 --> 00:05:55.300
Whoo!

61
00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:57.330
Feels good to see them lose!

62
00:05:57.360 --> 00:06:04.000
You bet! I hope they blow
that sorry sucker sky high!

63
00:06:04.040 --> 00:06:05.870
Wheeew...

64
00:06:05.910 --> 00:06:07.540
Naw I shouldn't say that.

65
00:06:07.580 --> 00:06:11.150
After all, Straw Hat's
our enemy too.

66
00:06:11.180 --> 00:06:14.980
I haven't beaten him
nearly enough, not yet.

67
00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:15.880
[FRANKY]
And to be fair.

68
00:06:15.920 --> 00:06:19.990
I was here first, wasn't I?

69
00:06:20.030 --> 00:06:23.360
I enjoyed your little
show but this's my stage

70
00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:27.190
and the only
star here is Franky.

71
00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:30.860
So get out of my way!

72
00:06:30.860 --> 00:06:33.730
Galley-la!

73
00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:34.600
[KAKU]
Hold your horses.

74
00:06:34.630 --> 00:06:36.040
We'll be done
with him in a second.

75
00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:38.980
Then you can fight us
to your heart's content.

76
00:06:39.010 --> 00:06:42.040
Listen, you. I called
dibs on Straw Hat

77
00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:45.120
before all of you
even got here!

78
00:06:45.140 --> 00:06:46.530
No. Screw it.

79
00:06:46.530 --> 00:06:49.440
You don't even care what I say,
do you?

80
00:06:49.600 --> 00:06:50.720
[CITIZEN K]
Paulie! Watch out!

81
00:06:51.360 --> 00:06:53.030
[CITIZEN L]
Get outta there!

82
00:06:53.060 --> 00:06:56.330
[CITIZEN M]
Franky's going
nuts again! Run away!

83
00:06:56.400 --> 00:06:57.560
Huh?

84
00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:05.790
Connector Set.

85
00:07:05.870 --> 00:07:07.710
[chuckles]

86
00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:09.660
[CITIZEN O]
He brought down
a crane with that attack!

87
00:07:09.690 --> 00:07:10.960
It's lethal!

88
00:07:10.990 --> 00:07:13.100
[PAULIE]
That was him?

89
00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:14.260
[LULU]
Looks like a cannon hit it.

90
00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:16.630
[CITIZEN P]
He's about to fire!

91
00:07:16.630 --> 00:07:20.200
Get 'em bro, your
cannon's ready to go! Hey!

92
00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:23.540
Don't expect me to shoot a cannonball or
anything.

93
00:07:23.610 --> 00:07:26.710
The shells I fire are made of nothing but
air.

94
00:07:26.740 --> 00:07:30.580
Still these babies
break the speed of sound.

95
00:07:30.610 --> 00:07:34.150
Air, huh?

96
00:07:34.180 --> 00:07:36.050
[CITIZEN Q]
Run for your lives!

97
00:07:43.320 --> 00:07:44.610
What the hell?

98
00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:50.670
Auuuuuuuuuhhhhh!

99
00:07:51.230 --> 00:07:52.490
Augh!

100
00:07:52.490 --> 00:07:54.690
Coup de Vent!

101
00:08:19.980 --> 00:08:22.780
[CROWD screams]

102
00:08:27.760 --> 00:08:29.120
[chuckles]

103
00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:39.480
Man, he wasn't kidding,

104
00:08:39.520 --> 00:08:42.020
that thing hits like a
hurricane to the face.

105
00:08:42.710 --> 00:08:45.130
[CITIZEN R]
Another
crane is coming down!

106
00:08:45.140 --> 00:08:48.910
[CITIZEN S]
Get outta here!
It's gonna fall on us!

107
00:08:51.910 --> 00:08:52.610
[CITIZEN T]
Hurry up!

108
00:08:52.610 --> 00:08:53.780
[CITIZEN U]
Here it comes!

109
00:08:55.650 --> 00:08:57.590
Hahahaha!

110
00:08:57.620 --> 00:08:59.690
Yeah! Let it fall!

111
00:09:00.780 --> 00:09:02.020
[FRANKY]
Hell, I don't care!

112
00:09:02.050 --> 00:09:05.720
Let's bring the whole damn shipyard down!

113
00:09:21.960 --> 00:09:23.100
He really is a cyborg!

114
00:09:23.130 --> 00:09:26.330
I thought he was kidding but
that air shot was no joke.

115
00:09:26.380 --> 00:09:29.350
I've never even seen
technology like that!

116
00:09:29.470 --> 00:09:30.640
B-But hey...

117
00:09:30.640 --> 00:09:32.310
No more angry mob at least.

118
00:09:34.350 --> 00:09:35.850
[LUFFY]
Nami! Run!

119
00:09:35.850 --> 00:09:36.640
Luffy!

120
00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:39.780
You didn't get hit back there,
did you?

121
00:09:39.810 --> 00:09:41.110
It's gonna take a
lot more than that

122
00:09:41.150 --> 00:09:43.780
if those guys
wanna get rid of me!

123
00:09:45.080 --> 00:09:47.330
Okay, come on.
We need to get going.

124
00:09:47.330 --> 00:09:49.840
I'm not sure how, but
we've gotta talk to Ice Pops.

125
00:09:49.870 --> 00:09:51.700
What? Now?

126
00:09:51.740 --> 00:09:54.610
When the whole town is out searching for
us?

127
00:09:54.640 --> 00:09:55.810
[CITIZEN V]
Hey! Look!

128
00:09:55.850 --> 00:09:57.780
Straw Hat is getting away!

129
00:09:57.820 --> 00:09:58.850
Uh-oh.

130
00:09:58.950 --> 00:10:00.880
They're trying to surround us.

131
00:10:01.520 --> 00:10:02.220
Nami.

132
00:10:02.220 --> 00:10:03.590
Huh?

133
00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:07.920
Better hold on tight, okay?

134
00:10:08.090 --> 00:10:10.160
No, not okay!

135
00:10:10.190 --> 00:10:11.290
[CITIZEN W]
Stop them!

136
00:10:17.270 --> 00:10:17.970
[CITIZEN X]
They're too fast!

137
00:10:17.970 --> 00:10:19.870
[CITIZEN]
Follow them!

138
00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:25.600
[KIWI]
Bro?

139
00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:27.100
[FRANKY]
Hm?

140
00:10:27.440 --> 00:10:28.210
[KIWI]
They're getting away.

141
00:10:28.240 --> 00:10:30.980
Don't you want to go after them?

142
00:10:31.010 --> 00:10:35.150
Nah that last Coupe de Vent
I did ate up all my fuel.

143
00:10:35.180 --> 00:10:37.990
You see this?
My pompadour's limp.

144
00:10:38.020 --> 00:10:41.660
No kidding. It looks like
a willow swaying in the wind.

145
00:10:43.060 --> 00:10:45.860
What a mess. Stupid Galley-La.

146
00:10:45.890 --> 00:10:49.400
I'll take care of that Straw Hat
as soon as I'm done refueling.

147
00:10:49.490 --> 00:10:51.830
Hahaha.

148
00:10:51.880 --> 00:10:54.080
But that kid ain't
half bad, y'know.

149
00:10:54.120 --> 00:10:59.660
He certainly earned
his big bounty. Hahahaha!

150
00:11:01.900 --> 00:11:04.500
[KAKU]
Geeze Louise.

151
00:11:04.530 --> 00:11:07.100
Even for Franky
this is too much.

152
00:11:07.130 --> 00:11:09.200
Today just isn't our day.

153
00:11:09.240 --> 00:11:10.700
[PAULIE]
Franky or no Franky,

154
00:11:10.740 --> 00:11:12.940
we can't let Straw Hat escape.

155
00:11:12.940 --> 00:11:15.780
Aqua Laguna is gonna hit tonight.

156
00:11:15.810 --> 00:11:19.080
There are only two Sea Train
departures left today.

157
00:11:19.080 --> 00:11:21.780
Since the Straw Hats
can't leave on their ship

158
00:11:21.820 --> 00:11:22.830
the Sea Train's the only ticket

159
00:11:22.830 --> 00:11:25.180
they've got to get off the island.

160
00:11:25.180 --> 00:11:26.750
This is our chance.

161
00:11:26.870 --> 00:11:29.200
Have every member
of Galley-La spread out

162
00:11:29.240 --> 00:11:31.060
and hunt them down.

163
00:11:31.150 --> 00:11:32.820
We'll settle this before sunset.

164
00:11:46.520 --> 00:11:49.440
Granny, look! It's Water Seven!

165
00:11:51.680 --> 00:11:56.990
Don't get too excited
and fall in the ocean now!

166
00:11:57.020 --> 00:12:00.260
[train whistle blowing]

167
00:12:07.800 --> 00:12:10.730
If that isn't Galley-La HQ, I don't know
what is.

168
00:12:10.840 --> 00:12:15.410
No surprise since it's right
next to Dock One. And look.

169
00:12:15.440 --> 00:12:18.380
The place is totally swarming with
reporters.

170
00:12:18.410 --> 00:12:22.420
Those tough-looking guys are probably
shipwrights.

171
00:12:22.450 --> 00:12:25.490
I'm willing to bet
that's where Iceburg's at.

172
00:12:28.380 --> 00:12:29.440
You sure about this?

173
00:12:30.490 --> 00:12:31.460
Of course I am.

174
00:12:31.490 --> 00:12:33.530
The only way for me to
find out what's going on

175
00:12:33.560 --> 00:12:36.970
between Ice Pops and
Robin is to ask him myself.

176
00:12:37.000 --> 00:12:39.070
I can't stop you but
you should keep in mind

177
00:12:39.100 --> 00:12:40.440
that everyone
on the island

178
00:12:40.470 --> 00:12:42.500
is trying to hunt
us down right now.

179
00:12:42.500 --> 00:12:44.800
So listen, before
you do anything rash,

180
00:12:44.830 --> 00:12:46.840
sneak around and figure
out where Iceburg's room

181
00:12:46.870 --> 00:12:49.570
is so you know
where you need to go.

182
00:12:49.790 --> 00:12:51.130
[LUFFY]
All right, I'm off.

183
00:12:56.450 --> 00:12:57.560
What?! No!

184
00:12:57.590 --> 00:12:58.620
They can't find them.

185
00:12:58.660 --> 00:12:59.920
Huh?

186
00:13:05.600 --> 00:13:06.800
Who's that?!

187
00:13:06.860 --> 00:13:08.860
[SHIPWRIGHT B]
Wait! It can't be!

188
00:13:14.690 --> 00:13:16.440
[REPORTER A]
Someone broke the window!

189
00:13:18.740 --> 00:13:20.320
[SHIPWRIGHT A]
We're under attack!

190
00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:25.490
Straw Hat Luffy broke in!
He must be after Iceburg!

191
00:13:25.490 --> 00:13:27.700
He's doing this in
the middle of the day?!

192
00:13:27.960 --> 00:13:30.840
He's got some guts coming after us now!

193
00:13:30.840 --> 00:13:31.810
[SHIPWRIGHT E]
Where is he?

194
00:13:32.170 --> 00:13:34.130
He's taking the stairs up to the third
floor!

195
00:13:34.130 --> 00:13:35.420
[SHIPWRIGHT G]
Where are the foremen?!

196
00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:37.040
[SHIPWRIGHT H]
They all spread
out looking for Straw Hat!

197
00:13:37.040 --> 00:13:38.710
No one is here!

198
00:13:40.280 --> 00:13:43.020
[SHIPWRIGHT J]
He's wearing
a red vest! You can't miss him!

199
00:13:43.040 --> 00:13:45.810
[SHIPWRIGHT K]
Don't
let him get to Iceburg!

200
00:13:47.010 --> 00:13:48.750
[SHIPWRIGHT L]
I found him!

201
00:13:50.680 --> 00:13:51.850
[sighs]

202
00:13:51.880 --> 00:13:53.980
[SHIPWRIGHT M]
Hey! Over here!

203
00:13:54.730 --> 00:13:56.360
Where is he? Where is he?

204
00:14:05.800 --> 00:14:07.560
[SHIPWRIGHT N]
Don't shoot a pistol, you idiot!

205
00:14:07.580 --> 00:14:10.820
We're inside! You're
gonna disturb Mr. Iceburg!

206
00:14:13.050 --> 00:14:14.790
[KALIFA]
I know you need to rest.

207
00:14:14.840 --> 00:14:16.710
I apologize for the commotion.

208
00:14:16.710 --> 00:14:19.130
[ICEBURG]
Mmwell, what's going on?

209
00:14:19.810 --> 00:14:23.470
Apparently, Straw Hat Luffy has
broken in and is running amuck.

210
00:14:25.820 --> 00:14:29.150
In that case. I have a plan.

211
00:14:32.290 --> 00:14:33.090
[SHIPWRIGHT O]
Found him!

212
00:14:33.120 --> 00:14:33.960
[LUFFY]
Uh-oh!

213
00:14:36.570 --> 00:14:38.800
[LUFFY]
Whoa, that's
a lotta shipwrights.

214
00:14:39.470 --> 00:14:41.540
[SHIPWRIGHT P]
He's going
to building 2! Follow him!

215
00:14:48.210 --> 00:14:49.580
Luffy, wait!

216
00:14:53.820 --> 00:14:55.020
It's you.

217
00:14:56.790 --> 00:14:59.160
[SHIPWRIGHT Q]
Kalifa, did you
see a pirate come this way?

218
00:14:59.190 --> 00:15:00.990
If I had, then you'd know.

219
00:15:01.030 --> 00:15:03.460
And by the way, you're far too noisy.

220
00:15:03.460 --> 00:15:06.450
Mr. Iceburg still needs
his peace and quiet.

221
00:15:06.450 --> 00:15:08.180
[SHIPWRIGHT Q]
You're right. Sorry.

222
00:15:08.220 --> 00:15:10.320
Looks like the Straw Hat hasn't made it
this far yet.

223
00:15:10.570 --> 00:15:11.720
Let's stand watch
around this hallway.

224
00:15:12.420 --> 00:15:14.390
This is where he's headed for sure.

225
00:15:25.020 --> 00:15:27.830
Mwell hello there, Pirate Boy.

226
00:15:27.860 --> 00:15:29.900
Were you looking for me?

227
00:15:29.930 --> 00:15:33.660
Sure was. Thanks for
saving me from those guys.

228
00:15:33.700 --> 00:15:35.070
[ICEBURG]
Considering the angry mob.

229
00:15:35.100 --> 00:15:38.300
I assume that you didn't
burst in here just to murder me.

230
00:15:38.340 --> 00:15:41.960
[LUFFY]
All I want is to
hear your side of the story!

231
00:15:41.960 --> 00:15:46.000
Last night. I saw Nico
Robin here, without a doubt.

232
00:15:48.150 --> 00:15:51.120
And mind you. I have
nothing against any of you.

233
00:15:51.150 --> 00:15:53.290
I have no reason to lie.

234
00:15:53.320 --> 00:15:55.690
Are you sure it wasn't someone who looked
like her?

235
00:15:55.720 --> 00:15:57.990
[ICEBURG]
Shut up and listen, boy.

236
00:15:58.710 --> 00:16:02.180
I didn't call you in here to bicker about
who did what.

237
00:16:02.790 --> 00:16:04.830
I have a favor to ask
and it would be

238
00:16:04.860 --> 00:16:07.400
in your best
interest to grant it.

239
00:16:08.570 --> 00:16:10.470
[ICEBURG]
No matter what it takes.

240
00:16:10.500 --> 00:16:12.900
I have to see Nico Robin again!

241
00:16:12.410 --> 00:16:18.250
<b>Blue Station</b>

242
00:16:14.520 --> 00:16:15.920
[CHIMNEY]
We're here! We're here!

243
00:16:15.950 --> 00:16:18.050
Come on, Granny, Hurry! Hurry!

244
00:16:18.090 --> 00:16:21.020
[KOKORO]
Calm down,
get a hold of yourself.

245
00:16:22.690 --> 00:16:23.930
Aaah...

246
00:16:24.170 --> 00:16:27.720
Water Seven, it's been a while.

247
00:16:27.720 --> 00:16:30.090
[CHIMNEY]
Granny! Hurry! Hurry!

248
00:16:30.090 --> 00:16:31.090
Okay, okay.

249
00:16:32.100 --> 00:16:33.840
[STATION AGENT A]
Attention, all passengers!

250
00:16:33.870 --> 00:16:36.810
Wearing a mask on the sea train
today is strictly prohibited!

251
00:16:36.810 --> 00:16:39.140
Look, ma'am, just cooperate
and show me your face.

252
00:16:39.140 --> 00:16:41.190
This is my face, see?

253
00:16:42.400 --> 00:16:43.320
Huh?

254
00:16:43.900 --> 00:16:45.190
[KOKORO]
Hey, you!

255
00:16:45.620 --> 00:16:48.360
Oh... Uh, Ms. Kokoro!
So nice to see you again!

256
00:16:48.390 --> 00:16:50.700
What's going on here? Trouble?

257
00:16:50.730 --> 00:16:51.830
[STATION AGENT C]
Yes, yes, ma'am.

258
00:16:51.860 --> 00:16:53.110
Everyone is on the lookout
for the Straw Hat pirates.

259
00:16:53.110 --> 00:16:54.510
The Straw Hat Pirates
were the culprits

260
00:16:54.550 --> 00:16:57.320
in the attack
against Mr. Iceburg!

261
00:17:07.670 --> 00:17:11.240
[ICEBURG]
I'll say it once again.

262
00:17:11.270 --> 00:17:13.880
Let me see Nico Robin!

263
00:17:13.910 --> 00:17:17.250
[LUFFY]
Sorry, that's not possible.

264
00:17:17.280 --> 00:17:20.920
We have no idea where she is.

265
00:17:20.950 --> 00:17:22.420
[loud gunshot]

266
00:17:26.360 --> 00:17:27.150
[CRAFTSMAN A]
Gunfire!

267
00:17:27.940 --> 00:17:29.440
It came from the bedroom!

268
00:17:34.350 --> 00:17:36.450
[CRAFTSMAN A]
Iceburg, we heard a...?!

269
00:17:42.660 --> 00:17:45.530
Are... Are you all right?

270
00:17:45.580 --> 00:17:47.420
Yes.

271
00:17:47.510 --> 00:17:49.610
I'd hoped to come
closer to the truth

272
00:17:49.650 --> 00:17:52.680
but that foolish
hope has been in vain.

273
00:17:52.720 --> 00:17:56.020
Arrest all of the Straw Hat Pirates.

274
00:17:56.060 --> 00:17:57.730
[CRAFTSMAN B]
Yes, sir!

275
00:18:01.520 --> 00:18:02.890
[NAMI]
Hey, Luffy.

276
00:18:03.020 --> 00:18:04.820
Were you able to
speak with Iceburg?

277
00:18:04.850 --> 00:18:06.760
What did he say? Is it true?

278
00:18:06.790 --> 00:18:09.730
Yeah he said it was
Robin, no doubt of it.

279
00:18:09.760 --> 00:18:10.860
No way! Why would...?

280
00:18:10.860 --> 00:18:13.110
Why would she do something like that?

281
00:18:13.110 --> 00:18:15.110
I refuse to believe it!

282
00:18:16.370 --> 00:18:18.700
<b>Main Street
Water Seven</b>

283
00:18:35.810 --> 00:18:38.110
Hey there!
Welcome! How are you?

284
00:18:38.140 --> 00:18:41.310
Ow! How's everything
going, Blueno?

285
00:18:41.340 --> 00:18:45.150
Feeling super?

286
00:18:45.180 --> 00:18:46.580
Eh heh heh heh...

287
00:18:46.620 --> 00:18:48.720
Yeah, well, I suppose you could say that.

288
00:18:48.800 --> 00:18:50.530
[FRANKY]
What do you mean "suppose"?

289
00:18:50.600 --> 00:18:53.140
You're not a very decisive guy,
are you?

290
00:18:53.170 --> 00:18:55.840
I'll take the usual.
Fill 'er up, please!

291
00:18:56.160 --> 00:18:58.120
Do you got any money?

292
00:18:58.120 --> 00:19:00.790
Just fill 'em up,
will ya?! Cola!

293
00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:03.440
Gah! To think that you run
an establishment like this

294
00:19:03.520 --> 00:19:06.460
with the greedy notion of taking
money from your customers!

295
00:19:06.490 --> 00:19:07.860
We do have a little money.

296
00:19:07.890 --> 00:19:10.360
About a million berries left from our
shopping spree.

297
00:19:10.410 --> 00:19:12.280
What?!

298
00:19:12.290 --> 00:19:14.760
We have that much left?!
How disgraceful!

299
00:19:14.800 --> 00:19:16.470
How totally uncool!

300
00:19:16.510 --> 00:19:19.420
To think that I didn't spend it all in one
night!

301
00:19:19.450 --> 00:19:21.420
Here! Gimme that!

302
00:19:21.510 --> 00:19:24.950
Ow! Listen up! This is
your lucky day, customers!

303
00:19:24.950 --> 00:19:26.320
All of your drinks are on me!

304
00:19:26.360 --> 00:19:28.460
Knock back as much
booze as you like!

305
00:19:28.490 --> 00:19:31.260
Complements of me,
your pal, Franky!

306
00:19:32.580 --> 00:19:35.540
[CUSTOMER A]
That's our
Franky! You're the best!

307
00:19:35.540 --> 00:19:37.770
[CUSTOMER B]
The face of
Water Seven's underworld!

308
00:19:37.770 --> 00:19:39.540
What a guy!

309
00:19:39.580 --> 00:19:41.510
[CUSTOMER C]
Whoa!
That's awesome!

310
00:19:41.540 --> 00:19:43.610
[CUSTOMER D]
Look over here!
It's piled up on the floor!

311
00:19:43.640 --> 00:19:45.780
[FRANKY]
So, Blueno! Where's my cola?

312
00:19:45.810 --> 00:19:47.880
Come on! Hurry it up, already!

313
00:19:47.990 --> 00:19:50.860
[KOKORO]
Looks like business
has been good for you, Franky.

314
00:19:50.890 --> 00:19:51.780
Huh?

315
00:19:51.780 --> 00:19:53.320
Ahh!

316
00:19:53.350 --> 00:19:56.890
Old hag Kokoro?!
That was you I sat next to?!

317
00:19:56.940 --> 00:20:00.310
I thought it was a
statue of a sea monster.

318
00:20:00.400 --> 00:20:02.660
Ahhh... Ahahahaha!

319
00:20:02.700 --> 00:20:03.600
[CHIMNEY]
Granny, is it okay

320
00:20:03.630 --> 00:20:06.770
for me to get a refill
on my juice then?

321
00:20:06.800 --> 00:20:08.300
Hey, kid, this is a bar.

322
00:20:08.340 --> 00:20:10.440
It's no place for little shrimps like you.

323
00:20:10.470 --> 00:20:12.240
[KOKORO]
Business has been good, right?

324
00:20:12.270 --> 00:20:15.910
Huh? Fine. Whatever.
Suit yourself.

325
00:20:15.960 --> 00:20:18.230
[CHIMNEY]
Hurray! Juice!

326
00:20:18.300 --> 00:20:20.330
Yeah, business has been outstanding.

327
00:20:20.370 --> 00:20:21.400
But I feel terrible.

328
00:20:21.440 --> 00:20:24.640
In fact, this entire week has been a total
downer.

329
00:20:24.670 --> 00:20:26.880
And it's all because of that stupid
pirate!

330
00:20:26.910 --> 00:20:28.440
[BLUENO]
Here you go! A full tank!

331
00:20:28.470 --> 00:20:30.440
[FRANKY]
Good! Took you long enough!

332
00:20:30.480 --> 00:20:33.810
Fuel, fuel, fuel, fuel!

333
00:20:33.850 --> 00:20:35.650
Mmmmmmm...

334
00:20:35.680 --> 00:20:39.450
Come on, come on, come on, come on!

335
00:20:50.110 --> 00:20:52.540
There! Completely restored!

336
00:20:52.580 --> 00:20:55.710
That bastard, wait 'til
I get my hands on him!

337
00:20:55.750 --> 00:20:58.450
Hey! Hag! Why are you here?

338
00:20:58.480 --> 00:21:00.550
Aqua Laguna is on its way.

339
00:21:00.580 --> 00:21:02.490
Oh? Is that right.

340
00:21:02.520 --> 00:21:04.860
No wonder the wind's blowing so strong
today.

341
00:21:04.890 --> 00:21:08.400
You need to get your house prepped up for
the storm.

342
00:21:08.430 --> 00:21:10.730
Well there's nothing
much to prep really,

343
00:21:10.760 --> 00:21:13.400
seeing as how I don't actually
have a house anymore.

344
00:21:13.450 --> 00:21:15.450
Hahahaha.

345
00:21:19.090 --> 00:21:21.490
[KOKORO]
I was going to
have a drink with Iceburg,

346
00:21:21.600 --> 00:21:24.530
but it seems he was shot.

347
00:21:24.530 --> 00:21:25.760
[FRANKY]
Yeah, I heard about that.

348
00:21:25.870 --> 00:21:27.770
They say pirates are responsible.

349
00:21:27.800 --> 00:21:30.070
Galley-La and the townspeople are raging
pissed.

350
00:21:30.070 --> 00:21:31.770
So a pirate did it, huh?

351
00:21:31.770 --> 00:21:32.010
Hahahaha!

352
00:21:32.010 --> 00:21:34.610
Do you honestly think that's what
happened?

353
00:21:36.320 --> 00:21:38.240
Hey, you sound like you know something.

354
00:21:38.550 --> 00:21:41.050
If you really do, then spit it out,
you old hag.

355
00:21:41.080 --> 00:21:44.090
Iceburg's constantly being
hounded by the World Government.

356
00:21:44.110 --> 00:21:45.210
You ever notice that?

357
00:21:45.240 --> 00:21:47.050
So? Wait, are you trying to say

358
00:21:47.080 --> 00:21:49.750
that government lap dog
Corgy pulled the trigger?

359
00:21:49.780 --> 00:21:50.980
Hahaha!

360
00:21:51.020 --> 00:21:53.820
That little troll isn't cut out to try
something like that.

361
00:21:53.880 --> 00:21:55.120
[KOKORO]
You're right.

362
00:21:55.120 --> 00:21:58.660
An assassination plot falls more
in line with the work of CP-9.

363
00:21:58.710 --> 00:22:01.280
Isn't that right, Blueno?
Ever heard of 'em?

364
00:22:01.290 --> 00:22:03.060
[BLUENO]
Eh...
Only rumors, really.

365
00:22:03.060 --> 00:22:05.000
Geez, you village
simpletons sure put

366
00:22:05.030 --> 00:22:06.570
a lot of stock
into stories about

367
00:22:06.670 --> 00:22:09.040
imaginary boogeyman-
shadow-organizations.

368
00:22:09.040 --> 00:22:11.770
[KOKORO]
Don't be an idiot.
Of course they exist.

369
00:22:11.810 --> 00:22:13.980
They just never show themselves.

370
00:22:14.010 --> 00:22:17.880
Can't really work undercover if everyone
knows who you are.

371
00:22:23.180 --> 00:22:24.990
You seem pretty sure of yourself.

372
00:22:25.020 --> 00:22:28.120
Got some kind of proof about this?

373
00:22:28.160 --> 00:22:31.190
Nope. Just rumors.
Nyahahaha!

374
00:22:31.230 --> 00:22:33.200
Stop screwing around, hag!

375
00:22:33.230 --> 00:22:35.530
Look, rumors are
superstitious nonsen...

376
00:22:35.560 --> 00:22:38.870
Strange they've remained a
rumor for such a long time, huh?

377
00:22:39.130 --> 00:22:42.510
They're good at eliminating people without
anyone noticing.

378
00:22:42.860 --> 00:22:45.600
If you mess with them, you're dead meat.

379
00:22:45.630 --> 00:22:52.440
Nyah! Hahahaha!

380
00:22:52.440 --> 00:22:54.110
[SHADOWED FIGURE]
Impressive work.

381
00:22:54.140 --> 00:22:58.550
The assignment we had to do yesterday went
very well.

382
00:22:58.580 --> 00:23:01.150
Excellent job, Nico Robin.

383
00:23:03.820 --> 00:23:05.530
Thanks. It was a cakewalk.

384
00:23:05.720 --> 00:23:06.950
[SHADOWED FIGURE]
Though, naturally,

385
00:23:07.000 --> 00:23:08.100
you're now being pursued

386
00:23:08.140 --> 00:23:10.840
by every last
person in the city.

387
00:23:10.870 --> 00:23:11.870
[ROBIN]
Indeed, I am.

388
00:23:11.910 --> 00:23:15.180
[SHADOWED FIGURE]
Merely a temporary setback.

389
00:23:15.220 --> 00:23:19.220
Tonight is what's
important. Understand?

390
00:23:19.540 --> 00:23:22.260
We'll infiltrate Iceburg's
residence one more time.

391
00:23:22.590 --> 00:23:24.690
If it becomes a
worst-case scenario,

392
00:23:24.730 --> 00:23:27.930
you're free to eliminate
all of the evidence.

393
00:23:27.960 --> 00:23:30.060
Among Tom's apprentices
who could've had it

394
00:23:30.090 --> 00:23:31.660
from the very beginning,

395
00:23:31.690 --> 00:23:35.700
Iceburg is the only
one that remains alive.

396
00:23:35.730 --> 00:23:37.970
No matter how much
he denies having it,

397
00:23:38.270 --> 00:23:42.190
in the name of CP9,
we will take it tonight.

398
00:23:43.030 --> 00:23:47.530
Never forget... this is
a mission of justice.
